---
/**
 * Supporting Editorial Content for HEIC to JPG Converter
 *
 * Provides educational context on the HEIC format, compatibility considerations,
 * practical conversion scenarios, and verified client-side privacy assurances.
 */
---

<div class="space-y-14 mb-14">
  <!-- 1. What is a HEIC file? -->
  <section aria-labelledby="what-is-heic-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-blue-100 text-blue-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          i
        </div>
        <h2 id="what-is-heic-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
          What is a HEIC file?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-surface-600 leading-relaxed max-w-none">
        <p>
          HEIC stands for High Efficiency Image Container, an image specification based on the broader High Efficiency Image File Format (HEIF) standard created by the Moving Picture Experts Group (MPEG). The format gained widespread adoption after Apple made it the default photo capture format across iPhone and iPad devices, but it is an open industry standard supported across numerous cameras and modern platforms.
        </p>
        <p>
          HEIC is engineered to store high-resolution photographs with advanced compression algorithms that often reduce file storage requirements by up to fifty percent compared to legacy image formats at comparable visual clarity. It can encapsulate multiple frames, auxiliary depth maps, transparency channels, and 16-bit color data within a single container.
        </p>
        <p>
          Despite these efficiency benefits, HEIC is not yet universal. Many older operating systems, web upload portals, email clients, photo editors, and school or workplace submission forms still expect standard JPEG files. Converting a HEIC image to JPG restores instant compatibility across virtually every device and software workflow. Explore our broader suite of <a href="/image" class="text-brand-600 font-medium underline decoration-brand-300 underline-offset-2 hover:text-brand-700 transition-colors">in-browser image tools</a> for other private conversion tasks.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Why convert HEIC to JPG? -->
  <section aria-labelledby="why-convert-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-3">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          ⇄
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 id="why-convert-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
            Why convert HEIC to JPG?
          </h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 mt-0.5">Everyday scenarios where standard JPEG remains the practical choice</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-6">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span>
            Web Forms & Document Portals
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Government submission forms, job application portals, university uploads, and banking verification systems frequently restrict file uploads to standard JPG or PNG extensions.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-500"></span>
            Cross-Platform Sharing
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Sending photos to recipients using older Windows PCs, legacy Android builds, or Linux setups can result in unreadable attachments unless specialized codecs are manually installed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Desktop Software & Office Suites
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Older desktop photo organizers, word processors, slide deck software, and creative editing utilities often struggle to import or display HEIC containers directly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200/70">
          <h3 class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 mb-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500"></span>
            Photo Printing Kiosks
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Retail photo kiosks, automated pharmacy printers, and local print shops routinely expect standard JPEG files on flash drives or memory cards for automated order processing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Privacy Guarantee Callout -->
  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-guarantee-heading">
    <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-50/80 border border-emerald-200 text-emerald-950 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3.5">
        <div class="p-2 rounded-xl bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75m-3-7.036A11.959 11.959 0 013.598 6 11.99 11.99 0 003 9.749c0 5.592 3.824 10.29 9 11.623 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.31-.21-2.571-.598-3.751h-.152c-3.196 0-6.1-1.248-8.25-3.285z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 id="privacy-guarantee-heading" class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-emerald-900">
            Privacy Notice: 100% Client-Side File Processing
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-emerald-800 mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
            Unlike online file converters that upload your private photos to remote servers for processing, this tool executes entirely inside your web browser. Your photo contents and filenames are never transmitted across the network, stored on remote disks, or inspected by third parties. Converted JPGs remain exclusively in your local device memory until you download them.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
